of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278478/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7619/selection/69a727252393c0c8196201a179547952561d9a510427fa35e0abcfe179db9a9d" :answer/id #uuid "43bd5ea6-0301-56e9-8c7c-a1b548a2ae67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7619/selection/d76e97b67fad2d42c4d5fc5117f14e01ca613b477338c64bbc5b3e3ae43fdda3" :answer/id #uuid "b647881b-35ee-58f9-8155-a91a17254dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7619/selection/ff19a3590848e1befeb4c176153b27e872ed61abbe5f77fef2dde0b8c0804f0a" :answer/id #uuid "28ca37b7-8d58-5047-bcf6-c186bfa39cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{9}+(y-2)^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7619/selection/bed182edf1e2a2d98eb230144d06f4b203bb4fc203ac8487b934819e757b6ced" :answer/id #uuid "9add08b1-8336-57b1-9572-81bf40396815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer