$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7619/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7619"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278254/field-1/bccffdc6e7d742a146fb440a695fb692d064aecfd1e3e85190f30a613646b055" :answer/id #uuid "7d972cb7-f674-5723-919a-f6d3dc0421ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278254/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed274ac7-35bf-5a13-8527-60067f477907" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278254/field-1/bccffdc6e7d742a146fb440a695fb692d064aecfd1e3e85190f30a613646b055" :answer-field/choices ["q-278254/field-1/bccffdc6e7d742a146fb440a695fb692d064aecfd1e3e85190f30a613646b055"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278254" :question/id #uuid "01c8b954-6543-5e80-b060-0261735b6399" :question/math-academy-id "q-278254" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/assets/65a76a438b3459a92db0e00b0c9bd281b8a9c58fa68afd2d8e6468a1d99b1cf9.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278254/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278388/field-1/1693137b9e761b4fa7f8a03b1fe4f8a4467df18b20ee4d5993cc8fef711b6e66" :answer/id #uuid "fe076377-8319-5645-a6ba-da20eaf3197e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278388/field-1/404ae8ab94bfb6bb9db7fd17f0e411101f5b22298dd2c89fed183f23a7e639fa" :answer/id #uuid "77f37205-cdd0-5c13-b381-5ff81058df31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278388/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "86eeb558-0a17-5eec-92c7-1bda3882a012" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278388/field-1/1693137b9e761b4fa7f8a03b1fe4f8a4467df18b20ee4d5993cc8fef711b6e66" :answer-field/choices ["q-278388/field-1/1693137b9e761b4fa7f8a03b1fe4f8a4467df18b20ee4d5993cc8fef711b6e66" "q-278388/field-1/404ae8ab94bfb6bb9db7fd17f0e411101f5b22298dd2c89fed183f23a7e639fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278388" :question/id #uuid "9bf6e24e-9e09-52c8-ac2f-212d781bbce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-278388" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/assets/8d6064ed62a5bdac5bac8c77e58617a5179d71ffe6cd0dc25f902af5e56bae07.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278388/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection/167e5b78d85bc6aaadb65232c7d212db7811ee734eae322d4e759b1bab639a98" :answer/id #uuid "34628de9-258f-5d53-909a-59d1d21e2165" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection/49b905c56039899f273faa6b3b021aeb63993b4b3125603150712a17495bea9d" :answer/id #uuid "6df25aa2-352c-5495-8216-5c1dbfaa84a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection/69875022ea24dab789acb9aa9586825c66187480f51b28c34560fb70324331b9" :answer/id #uuid "846fb119-bb52-5c4d-83be-e8bee1e23474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection/f2d748c1305fde0e9f4f7bcb918b62060344d7f348e58f4511aa617eff72a7db" :answer/id #uuid "47888f8c-586d-5488-99e1-8e5fc39b4493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection/1a9ba448a31063dd77c789c781ec6d0b1984b5d9bb71288a96ececdd23b0edee" :answer/id #uuid "b581842c-4283-59cf-b828-367c0105818f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef84a0d9-abca-59e6-9dfb-84329e3f1050" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16553/selection/49b905c56039899f273faa6b3b021aeb63993b4b3125603150712a17495bea9d" :answer-field/choices ["q-16553/selection/167e5b78d85bc6aaadb65232c7d212db7811ee734eae322d4e759b1bab639a98" "q-16553/selection/49b905c56039899f273faa6b3b021aeb63993b4b3125603150712a17495bea9d" "q-16553/selection/69875022ea24dab789acb9aa9586825c66187480f51b28c34560fb70324331b9" "q-16553/selection/f2d748c1305fde0e9f4f7bcb918b62060344d7f348e58f4511aa617eff72a7db" "q-16553/selection/1a9ba448a31063dd77c789c781ec6d0b1984b5d9bb71288a96ececdd23b0edee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16553" :question/id #uuid "7b22ea02-8b75-5f49-8c84-897dbc1c2b11" :question/math-academy-id "q-16553" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/assets/0efd7cec177f27696620bba018055fb6c834823d3c13413b325b4d69095e07dd.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=1,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-16553/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection/fab95e591ce7e8de3946f5bc5df86f4be42b3aa1a51233f6a4da1f10e6ec7c3c" :answer/id #uuid "e92be744-a538-5e8e-8575-cf982b7165c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection/d68d300b84531634e99e2a437e8ec570cce0330eddf6035b4e4bc757a32b5636" :answer/id #uuid "236f14d7-96f1-5754-ada4-0b63acc9f922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection/e81329609fdea7659a2b4531afb115e30ae7d2354769a66382e4f57b03cd8fbe" :answer/id #uuid "18dbd1de-338c-50e0-a5b2-c658362e911e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection/5e17646a908cb8ad6fae4a3fad326c8432c362b27429581a5b0a69b0f5363d9f" :answer/id #uuid "78c3f94c-c4a9-5bf9-80f4-462cd2099cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection/0b162304c80e107f932024d8318e1bc4bdb7be7b2b44cdddd2aa5a8d959eae33" :answer/id #uuid "ed361dfa-6b16-5d9d-b7cb-81007146a4bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f66672-6bc0-5b5e-bf3b-cd857be4351f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115297/selection/e81329609fdea7659a2b4531afb115e30ae7d2354769a66382e4f57b03cd8fbe" :answer-field/choices ["q-115297/selection/fab95e591ce7e8de3946f5bc5df86f4be42b3aa1a51233f6a4da1f10e6ec7c3c" "q-115297/selection/d68d300b84531634e99e2a437e8ec570cce0330eddf6035b4e4bc757a32b5636" "q-115297/selection/e81329609fdea7659a2b4531afb115e30ae7d2354769a66382e4f57b03cd8fbe" "q-115297/selection/5e17646a908cb8ad6fae4a3fad326c8432c362b27429581a5b0a69b0f5363d9f" "q-115297/selection/0b162304c80e107f932024d8318e1bc4bdb7be7b2b44cdddd2aa5a8d959eae33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115297" :question/id #uuid "88a83a53-4b54-5fb6-8023-0cc5bd988bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115297" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/assets/1006eabe3321beb48df2cd936ff2252b77e8ded81f9c5b7aec4d143e43941088.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-4,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115297/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278402/field-1/d253ac0ac20b641e12f953f9412aa9f9d95729120756fea738c6358f9fcb04d9" :answer/id #uuid "97a56b89-7939-55e5-aa7f-0de277930e6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278402/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a3e32c-7502-5d12-a165-e06a2e52dcdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278402/field-1/d253ac0ac20b641e12f953f9412aa9f9d95729120756fea738c6358f9fcb04d9" :answer-field/choices ["q-278402/field-1/d253ac0ac20b641e12f953f9412aa9f9d95729120756fea738c6358f9fcb04d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278402/field-2/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "375397a9-b308-5964-af77-9cc319b096b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278402/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d3002bc-bbe1-5c58-b61e-5c7eeded7b0d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278402/field-2/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer-field/choices ["q-278402/field-2/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278402" :question/id #uuid "b74a983b-5b3e-5c81-aeef-49a17e380aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-278402" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{11}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-7$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(-7,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=11.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=11,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{11}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{11},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{11}=2\\sqrt{11},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278402/field-1" "q-278402/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection/a9ba260b705994e64c5f11e6c174958b71d2a804e87864dafe0586f5647807e1" :answer/id #uuid "600683ff-0fc4-57eb-be3a-95ef45e63783" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12.5$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection/6b7da0c1c3b432f6cfbf1d6b13039eff49569989890489a8aa7ea5f0058aa42e" :answer/id #uuid "8266e82f-ea51-54aa-b30c-81394bcaa0a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection/0bd2db3e92494cf89b776d82aefb61b6f9dc92fe1440589a52ecf4114377311e" :answer/id #uuid "68efc7e8-3441-55ff-b591-6c2ac13efc7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ and $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection/2a8df328e31dedbd5beb0405315fd8033f3c51cbd6f7cdafe3342bf963f3c2d2" :answer/id #uuid "701f5a57-57a7-5b10-b7bf-8294bd1be08f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ and $2\\sqrt{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection/104f49b666e7259fd60a1cd90040a9ce45c5d9b7c5e4055cd3626c1ad80a54bb" :answer/id #uuid "2e99faa3-8566-5a6f-a7f3-fd094689f60d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "68cf1a26-32b1-5ade-a1c6-5c839bc90d21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115313/selection/2a8df328e31dedbd5beb0405315fd8033f3c51cbd6f7cdafe3342bf963f3c2d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-115313/selection/a9ba260b705994e64c5f11e6c174958b71d2a804e87864dafe0586f5647807e1" "q-115313/selection/6b7da0c1c3b432f6cfbf1d6b13039eff49569989890489a8aa7ea5f0058aa42e" "q-115313/selection/0bd2db3e92494cf89b776d82aefb61b6f9dc92fe1440589a52ecf4114377311e" "q-115313/selection/2a8df328e31dedbd5beb0405315fd8033f3c51cbd6f7cdafe3342bf963f3c2d2" "q-115313/selection/104f49b666e7259fd60a1cd90040a9ce45c5d9b7c5e4055cd3626c1ad80a54bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115313" :question/id #uuid "6821b43a-88ac-5b4b-9151-2f35f973a4c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115313" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-5$ and $k=2,$ so the center is located at $(-5,2).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=25$ and ${b}^{2}=6.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=25,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=6,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}=2\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115313/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115313"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115312/selection/c6c8afb08c7382c629164047fa9344b1a14000e7db59adc2907be78c2d9d36df" :answer/id #uuid "9c20f29b-dfe1-58eb-9af6-bc4727a6a082" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115312/selection/2d9cd23fe5d4f3625c30dccdc49798d9ed095c16137b9f8898c52a188e4e998b" :answer/id #uuid "adf73a4d-9982-5d4b-ac21-2c0249b86c04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115312/selection/9a72ca1dc47bf25f8c3aa0e227271ca50fb225e7541baa4aae4a32691ca11871" :answer