ation, we also have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=3.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=3,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115312/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115312"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection/e40e69bfc080e33178220330b9d792c4672c9869699292c9d9adbc655f9adfe0" :answer/id #uuid "84162d1a-da76-5322-b679-5d9d147be955" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection/851a90ce0e1b8c10716bfbe128073dea04aefb5ba6801b2662771bf79bd2961d" :answer/id #uuid "9e2b8d5b-204d-547e-9b2f-1597a2a9dbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection/97e148b0a2e2b4089f9a7d696d77c6133b643b69dcb2128f1a317b71c8bf1d94" :answer/id #uuid "ed738c7b-483b-56e8-a3b0-1c95058cfe3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection/af42c9cc34471d9892d026c29d104d494b09d4b0599bef2aaa4220cddff02606" :answer/id #uuid "fe487ffe-6654-55ee-9fa9-d3154382d03e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection/6a7004d084b2d346df9a3d8e434b1412014527000e696e6d1ef1af37e183d648" :answer/id #uuid "fa2581e0-79c6-519e-8744-4b424c92c926" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cce0e58f-a48b-56a7-87db-c9ef83a4c6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16465/selection/af42c9cc34471d9892d026c29d104d494b09d4b0599bef2aaa4220cddff02606" :answer-field/choices ["q-16465/selection/e40e69bfc080e33178220330b9d792c4672c9869699292c9d9adbc655f9adfe0" "q-16465/selection/851a90ce0e1b8c10716bfbe128073dea04aefb5ba6801b2662771bf79bd2961d" "q-16465/selection/97e148b0a2e2b4089f9a7d696d77c6133b643b69dcb2128f1a317b71c8bf1d94" "q-16465/selection/af42c9cc34471d9892d026c29d104d494b09d4b0599bef2aaa4220cddff02606" "q-16465/selection/6a7004d084b2d346df9a3d8e434b1412014527000e696e6d1ef1af37e183d648"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16465" :question/id #uuid "8cb21ae0-f2f0-5250-97c3-5094275c61e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-16465" :question/problem "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{20}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-1$ and $k=-3,$ so the center is located at $(-1,-3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=20.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=20,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-16465/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277200/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "d078fd87-3cca-57a7-9be9-d4bfea6c0de9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277200/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d44e0a4-d650-50e4-bb0f-f1f701607920" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277200/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-277200/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277200/field-2/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" :answer/id #uuid "6a5e8a0e-126a-5e65-9f50-dc6f94589ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277200/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9a0b25-e291-5708-805c-2a55b3815790" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277200/field-2/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" :answer-field/choices ["q-277200/field-2/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277200" :question/id #uuid "411c201c-8678-5df1-8612-44d7e43ee539" :question/math-academy-id "q-277200" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-4$ and $k=-3,$ so the center is located at $(-4,-3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=12.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=12,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-277200/field-1" "q-277200/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
